CTCToken.validPurchase() (../sb/0xe3fa177acecfb86721cf6f9f4206bd3bd672d7d5.sol#228-234) uses timestamp for comparisons
	Dangerous comparisons:
	- withinPeriod = getNow() >= startTime && getNow() <= endTime (../sb/0xe3fa177acecfb86721cf6f9f4206bd3bd672d7d5.sol#229)
	- withinPeriod && nonZeroPurchase && minContribution && notReachedHardCap (../sb/0xe3fa177acecfb86721cf6f9f4206bd3bd672d7d5.sol#233)
CTCToken.hasEnded() (../sb/0xe3fa177acecfb86721cf6f9f4206bd3bd672d7d5.sol#237-239) uses timestamp for comparisons
	Dangerous comparisons:
	- getNow() > endTime (../sb/0xe3fa177acecfb86721cf6f9f4206bd3bd672d7d5.sol#238)
Reference: https://github.com/crytic/slither/wiki/Detector-Documentation#block-timestamp

